{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123076","id":4414339486,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBx15ng","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123076","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123076.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123076.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123076","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123076/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123076/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123076/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/d6539fb8354e252b09912fe6c646af443234adb4","number":123076,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"GDShader: Display preprocessor errors instead of trying to compile non-preprocessed file","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #123056\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/pull_request_guidelines.html#explain-your-contributions\r\n-->\r\n\r\nPreviously, if shader preprocessing failed (such as due to an invalid path in an `#include` statement), the shader code as a whole would remain non-preprocessed before being compiled. Then, the compiler would see the `#` symbols from the preprocessor directives and fail on them. This meant that straightforward preprocessor errors would result in seemingly nonsensical error messages being displayed.\r\n\r\nThis PR saves the result of preprocessing, and checks to ensure the most recent preprocessing attempt was successful before attempting to compile the shader. If it was not successful, the error message from the preprocessor is displayed, and an empty shader is compiled in place of the broken, un-preprocessed shader supplied by the user.\r\n\r\nResults in the output panel using a modified version of the MRP for the issue linked above:\r\n| Without PR | With PR |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| <img width=\"447\" height=\"482\" alt=\"CleanShot 2026-09-01 at 09 40 01@2x\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b2b9cbb9-3233-4e3d-a175-e5f465d30b91\" /> | <img width=\"452\" height=\"232\" alt=\"CleanShot 2026-09-01 at 09 38 43@2x\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5ef05a7a-b6a5-4f40-a1c7-2abd176549e4\" /> |\r\n\r\nNotes:\r\n- I initially felt like I should include a similar code pattern in `ShaderInclude` (specifically, saving the result and possible error message of the preprocessor), but scanning through the codebase I didn't see anywhere that it would actually be applicable, so I left it be.\r\n- This error checking is currently not applied to cases in the engine where shaders are constructed such as the sky materials. ","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1609442062,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNjA5NDQyMDYy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:shaders","name":"topic:shaders","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gis